# Repositories and projects

- `internal/git` is a library (no HTTP). `Runner` owns the git binary, a minimal allowlisted environment (`filterEnv`), timeouts, size limits and per-operation sessions (private HOME, SSH key file, `ssh_config`, scrubbing log writer). Every command goes through `session.run`: `exec.CommandContext`, never a shell, `hardening()` `-c` options first, then the LFS filter and the LFS endpoint pin (`lfsPin`, when git-lfs exists), process-tree kill on cancel and after `Wait` (`proc_unix.go` with Linux `Pdeathsig`, `proc_windows.go` job object). Add new commands as `xxxArgs` functions and pin them in `TestArgv`.
- Invariants: validate URLs and branches with `ValidateRemoteURL`/`ValidateBranch` before use; positional arguments follow `--` or `--end-of-options`; credentials never go into argv, URLs, `.git/config` or logs (HTTPS via `GIT_ASKPASS` = the golem-deploy binary, see `Askpass`, wired first thing in `cmd/golem-deploy/main.go`; SSH via a 0600 key file in the session dir); everything written to the job log passes the `scrubber`; `Auth` renders without secrets in fmt and slog.
- Askpass answers only the exact prompt strings of `askpassPrompts` (configured host[:port] with explicit default-port and lower-case variants, user raw or percent-encoded like git); never loosen this to URL parsing.
- SSH options live only in the per-operation `ssh_config` (`sshConfig`, passed as `ssh -F <file>`); never pass paths through `-o`. Paths are double quoted with `%` doubled; `CheckSSHConfigPath` rejects what cannot be represented (the daemon checks the data dir at startup). SSH remotes always need a key (`CheckAuthKind`); the config sets `IdentityFile` explicitly, no agent, no password/keyboard-interactive.
- Git LFS: the endpoint is pinned from the project URL (`LFSEndpoint`: https -> `<url>[.git]/info/lfs`, SSH -> the remote) via `lfs.url` and `remote.origin.lfsurl` on the command line (outranks `.lfsconfig` and `.git/config`; git-lfs reads `lfs.url` first). Before `git lfs pull`, `checkLFSConfig` refuses a `.lfsconfig` with endpoint/transfer keys (`disallowedLFSKeys`, read with `git config --file`, symlinks refused) with `ReasonLFSConfig`. Then `lfsIncludes` calls `Options.LFSInclude` (the daemon passes `build.LFSInclude`, the contained reader and strict parser of `golem-deploy.yaml`; never parse the file in this package): patterns are re-checked (`checkLFSPatterns`) and passed as exactly one `--include=` argument (`lfsPullArgs`); an error fails the operation with `ReasonDeployConfig`, whose `Message` is the sanitised, clipped error text. Without the option or the key the command is plain `git lfs pull`.
- Limits: `Options.MaxRepoSize` (watchdog on clone, fetch, checkout, lfs pull via `cmdOpts.watch`, plus a check after each; `ReasonSizeLimit`), `MinFreeSpace` before clone/pull/branch (`ReasonDiskSpace`, `diskfree_*.go`).
- Failures are `*git.Error` with a `Reason` (classified from scrubbed English output, `LC_ALL=C`) and `Unchanged` (checkout untouched); show users only `Message()`/`SafeMessage`, never git output.
- Clone stages under the temp dir and renames into place; pull/branch = set-url, explicit fetch, `checkout --force -B`, `clean -ffdx`, then `git lfs pull` when `.gitattributes` uses `filter=lfs` (filter config is passed per command because global/system config is disabled).
- Before building, require idle status and compare `Runner.HeadCommit` with the recorded commit. An incomplete checkout needs a pull.
- Checkouts are `<datadir>/repositories/<project id>` (`git.CheckoutDir`), never derived from names. Delete through `git.RemoveCheckout` (containment check, symlinks not followed, moved aside first). `SweepTemp`/`SweepCheckouts` run at daemon startup.
- HTTP (`handlers_projects.go`): handlers depend on the `GitClient` interface (`Deps.Git`, nil means 503) so tests inject a fake. Job start and delete decisions hold `projectState.mu` (builds too); DELETE commits the database transaction before cleaning up the checkout and build images (builds rule); PATCH can set `static_addons` and `allow_custom_dockerfile`; jobs own the project status (transient on start; idle, previous or error on exit), read the project (URL, credentials) when they start running and update the row with `SetProjectCheckout`; PATCH uses `UpdateProjectRemote` and never runs git, and requires `auth` when the URL's origin changes (`git.SameOrigin`). Secrets are sealed with `secrets.ProjectAuthPurpose(id)` and only `auth_type`, `auth_username`, `has_secret` are returned.
- Integration tests serve bare repos over loopback HTTPS (`git http-backend` via `net/http/cgi`, CA via `GIT_SSL_CAINFO`, plus a minimal LFS batch API) and over an in-process `x/crypto/ssh` server (`ssh_integration_test.go`); `TestMain` makes the test binary the askpass helper. They skip when git, `git-http-backend`, `ssh` or `git-lfs` is missing. Security regressions are named `TestG<n>_...`; `proc_linux_test.go` only runs on Linux.
- Verify with `go test ./internal/git/... ./internal/httpapi/... ./internal/store/...`.
